## Systemic patterns swept (counts)
- `distint*` monoculture (ca-a 45, ca-b 28): 31 instances rewritten as `diferent*` — 26 in the columns (001 ×2, 002 ×3, 004 ×2, 006 ×1, 007 ×6, 008 ×1, 010 ×1, 011 ×1, 014 ×2, 016 ×4, 017 ×1, 018 was already fine) and 5 in the guidance pack. ~33 kept, all in the «distint de X» = “separate from / other than” sense, which is normal legal Catalan («no és una persona jurídica distinta de la seu», «persona distinta del cònjuge», «hereus legals distints del cònjuge»). `diferent` went from 1 occurrence to 32.
- `de forma + adjectiu` (ca-a 46, ca-b 32): all 149 occurrences in the 18 columns rewritten — 82 → the plain -ment adverb (automàticament, voluntàriament, conjuntament, individualment, directament, uniformement, lícitament, permanentment, mecànicament, reiteradament, periòdicament, unilateralment, intencionadament, definitivament, substancialment, arbitràriament, erròniament, recíprocament, indegudament, repetidament, contínuament, anticipadament, successivament, sistemàticament), 60 → `de manera + adjectiu` (kept as a phrase where the adverb shifts meaning: concreta, independent, general, continuada, coherent…), 7 rewritten individually (per escrit, greument, oficialment, a títol personal, vàlidament, dues vegades, satisfactòriament). `de forma` now appears 0 times in the columns. The guidance pack was deliberately left alone — see “rows skipped”.
- `veure` for examine: 17 instances (detail under ca-b 25).
- `tal com és`: 6 instances (detail under ca-a 36).
- Verbless clause after `sinó` / coordinating `i` (ca-b systemic): 6 instances — 016 ×3, 017 ×1, 001 ×1 («…sinó que s’ha de revisar de nou si cal una filial o una sucursal»), 014 ×1 («…sinó que s’han d’ordenar conjuntament les dades…»). The correct elliptical `sinó` (`sinó part de la seu`, `sinó requisits…`, `sinó qui signa…`, `sinó quin fonament…`) was left.
- Castilianisms subsanar / recolzar / bastar amb: 6 instances (011 ×2, 016 ×2, 018 ×1, 004 ×1). «bastar» used intransitively in 002 («si el patrimoni social no basta per pagar els deutes») is correct Catalan and was left; «pot no bastar» in 016 → «pot no ser suficient».
- Small cardinals as digits (ca-a 39): 9 instances written out, 4 reverted (below).
- Checks that needed no change: R4 gender (both reviewers found no masculine form for Wei Tseng; the male manager in 008 and the male client in 010 stay male), R5/R12 English chrome (already «EL NOSTRE EQUIP», «OFICINES»), R6b fullwidth punctuation (the only hits are inside Chinese glosses and inside the 008 frontmatter `url:`, which R16 exempts), consultation-language / advertising locks (both reviewers report them clean).

## Rows skipped (5) — with reason
- ca-a 16 P2 (003 Q16–Q20 should be `##` headings). SKIP: the `headings` check pins the heading-level array to the Korean source, which has Q16–Q20 as plain body text — source and target are both `levels=[1,2,…]` with 15 `##`. Promoting five lines to headings makes the checker FAIL. Writing them as `16.` instead would turn them into list items and break the `list items` count. Left as `**16.**`. (Structural defect inherited from the source; needs a supervisor decision if the outline is to be fixed.)
- ca-a 17 P2 / ca-b 12 P2 (delete the U+200B blank lines: 52 in 003, 8 in 005 incl. four `**​**`, 4 in 006, 10 in 008, 5 in 009, 5 in 013, 3 in 015). SKIP: `checkBlocks` compares the ZWSP count with the Korean source and the counts are already identical (003 52→52, 005 8→8, 006 4→4, 008 10→10, 009 5→5, 013 5→5, 015 3→3). Deleting them makes `blocks` FAIL on every one of those files, and the `**​**` lines are separate blocks in the source too, so removing them also changes the block count. This is a source-level defect that has to be fixed in `src/content/columns/` first.
- ca-a 38 P2 (bio «TWD 1.57M (1,57 milions de dòlars taiwanesos)» should be given once as «1,57 milions de dòlars de Taiwan»). SKIP per ACCEPTED-ROUND and R12: «TWD 1.57M» is pinned byte-identical by a test.
- ca-b 12 counted with ca-a 17 above.
- `de forma automàtica` in the guidance pack (7 occurrences, not a numbered row but part of ca-a 46/ca-b 32). NOT swept: `src/data/__tests__/guidance-disclosure-parity.test.ts` pins `ca: /de forma automàtica/` as the Catalan regex for the “text is not machine-translated” disclosure element. Rewriting those to `automàticament` would need the parity regex changed in the same edit; the work order limits test edits to expected strings of Catalan FAQ/title pins, so this was left for the supervisor. The pattern is fully swept in the 18 columns.

